    "title": "pandas.Index.identical — pandas 2.3.3 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Index.identical#\n\n- \n*final* Index.identical(*other* )[source]#\n- Similar to equals, but checks that object attributes and types are also equal. \n  - Returns:\n    - bool\n    - If two Index objects have equal elements and same type True, otherwise False.\n Examples >>> idx1 = pd.Index(['1', '2', '3']) >>> idx2 = pd.Index(['1', '2', '3']) >>> idx2.identical(idx1) True >>> idx1 = pd.Index(['1', '2', '3'], name=\"A\") >>> idx2 = pd.Index(['1', '2', '3'], name=\"B\") >>> idx2.identical(idx1) False",
    "markdown_length": 501,
